\textbf{Установка размера шрифта}

Standard font size is 10pt ($10$ points, or 12 pt with default article class). To change it:

\begin{tabular}{@{}ll@{}}
\toprule
\textbf{To achieve} & \textbf{Use} \\
\midrule
11pt & \verb|\documentclass[11pt]{article}|
12pt & \verb|\documentclass[12pt]{article}|
14pt & \verb|\documentclass[14pt]{extarticle}|
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}

\textbf{Кастомизация размеров шрифтов}

Custom font sizes can be created using the \verb|\fontsize{size}{baseline}{}|-command. Additionally, \verb|\enspace| and \verb|\quad| commands provide additional space.

\begin{tabular}{@{}ll@{}}
\toprule
\textbf{Size} & \textbf{Command} \\
\midrule
10pt & Default \\
11pt & \verb|\fontsize{11}{12}\selectfont| \\
12pt & \verb|\selectfont| \\
14pt & \verb|\fontsize{14}{16}\selectfont| \\
1em & \verb|\fontsize{\dimexpr 1em}{\fontsize-default-baseline}\selectfont|
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}

\textbf{Выравнивание текста}

LaTeX provides five standard ways to align text: left-aligned (\verb|\textleft|), right-aligned (\verb|\textright|), centered (\verb|\center|), justified (\verb|\begin{flushleft}\end{flushleft}| and \verb|\begin{flushright}\end{flushright}|), and aligned with respect to a specific point (\verb|\begin{flushleft}\end{flushleft}| and \verb|\begin{flushright}\end{flushright}| can also be used for one-sided justification).

